From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: explorer: the desktop shows its folders, selects, and has menus

The shell's desktop (0090) read the Desktop folders once and only for
shortcuts, and watched them in a way that never showed a new file: files
made there after sign-in never appeared, not even after F5 (QA B15). It now
shows every file and folder in the user's and the public Desktop folders
(shortcuts by their target's icon, other files by their type's), watches both
(names, folders, writes) and reads them again on the desktop's own thread a
moment after a burst of changes; F5 reads them again too.

It also behaves as a desktop (QA B16): a click selects an icon (drawn with a
translucent highlight) and a click on the empty desktop clears it; Enter
opens the selected icon. Right-clicking an icon opens its shell context menu
(Open, Send to, Cut, Copy, Delete, Rename, Properties ...). Right-clicking
the empty desktop, the menu key or Shift+F10 opens the desktop's menu:
View (Large, Medium, Small icons; Show desktop icons), Sort by (Name, Size,
Item type, Date modified; folders first), Refresh, New (Folder, Text
Document: made, named "New folder (2)" ... when taken, and selected),
Display settings (ms-settings:display) and Personalize
(ms-settings:personalization). The view is kept where the shell keeps it:
Shell\Bags\1\Desktop IconSize, Explorer\Advanced HideIcons, and
HKCU\Software\Stained Glass\Desktop SortBy.

The desktop window cannot be the foreground window, so keys never reached
it: a click on the desktop activates a 1x1 transparent tool window at the
screen's corner that passes F5, Enter and the menu keys to it and owns its
menus. The desktop draws itself before a menu opens (UpdateWindow only
erases the desktop window). SG_DESKTOP_DUMP names a file the desktop writes
its view, selection and icons to, for gates.

Gate: test/desktop-gate.sh (make test-desktop).
